Subject: [PATCH] clocksource: ingenic: support per-CPU and split OST blocks
Upstream-Status: Pending

Describe OST register layouts and clock capabilities per SoC. Add X1600,
X1700 and X1830 matching, plus separate 32-bit event and 64-bit global
blocks for newer X2000-family devices.

Allocate per-CPU clock events, initialize their register windows and
register the global counter as clocksource and sched_clock where available.

diff --git a/drivers/clocksource/ingenic-sysost.c b/drivers/clocksource/ingenic-sysost.c
index 026615bbe921f457e5ea0746fd128a35f491d967..fb5eb1662a17a31e2b56227d1b95778748714090 100644
--- a/drivers/clocksource/ingenic-sysost.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/ingenic-sysost.c
@@ -10,10 +10,13 @@
 #include <linux/clk-provider.h>
 #include <linux/clockchips.h>
 #include <linux/clocksource.h>
+#include <linux/cpuhotplug.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/syscon.h>
 #include <linux/of_address.h>
 #include <linux/of_irq.h>
+#include <linux/of_platform.h>
+#include <linux/overflow.h>
 #include <linux/sched_clock.h>
